  message: "Fixed in PR #2174 (dev, \"fix(sketch): Key Symbols draws from more files as the budget grows\", 2026-11-13). The ranked set is 20 files, or one for every three symbols of budget when that is more (sketch.key_symbol_file_limit); a file that holds an entry point and did not rank is admitted best score first, up to one for every four ranked files; ties in file score go by path. EVIDENCE, production path (hypergumbo sketch <repo> -t N, before on dev a5450bdd90 and after on the branch; Key Symbols file headings, and how many of the same sketch's top 30 Source Files are among them): hypergumbo 32k 47 (21/30) -> 46 (27/30) with script headings 12 -> 7; 128k 103 (21/30) -> 187 (29/30) with scripts 51 -> 22. alertmanager (Go) 32k 35 (22/30) -> 55 (26/30); 128k 38 (22/30) -> 157 (30/30). kserve (Python and Go, many small executables) 32k 60 (24/30) -> 54 (27/30); 128k 140 (25/30) -> 222 (30/30). The filed instance: taint.py, java.py, go.py, verify_claims.py and tui.py are under a Key Symbols heading at 32k and 128k (none before). 8k is unchanged on all three repos: the limit is 20 there as before, and the 8k sketch shows 16 symbols. Sketch length is unchanged (511,303 -> 511,842 characters at 128k). Five mutations of the rule each went red. NOT DONE: Key Symbols and Source Files still order files by two different scores (WI-zuroj); and at 128k hypergumbo's Key Symbols still has 5 headings inside the recorded fixture crate (WI-fosuk)."  # 201f
